// P03.20 (follow-up): category() (OWN-C1..C5) had a depth cut at 24 that
// answered Trivial, the unsafe side: S30 (30 named structs over a string) was
// Copy, so `t := s` copied a borrowed owner bitwise and NeedC[S30] satisfied
// Copy; R (a raw pointer next to S30) got an automatic Clone() that copies
// the pointer. Now the walk has no cut: S30 is owning like S5. The trivial
// chain P30 next to it stays Copy, and RP (a raw pointer next to P30) stays
// cloneable. Generic instances are answered from their declaration (its
// parameters held by value, joined with the arguments' categories): G30[T]
// holds T 30 levels down, so G30[string] and G30[Box[Mu]] are owning and
// G30[int] and G30[*Mu] are Copy; in a generic function G30[T] copies only
// when T is Copy.
// RUN: not %gopp check --check-error-limit=0 %s 2>&1 | FileCheck "--implicit-check-not=error[E" %s
package main

type NeedC[T Copy] struct{ v T }

type S0 struct{ s string }
type P0 struct{ x int }
type S1 struct{ in S0 }
type S2 struct{ in S1 }
type S3 struct{ in S2 }
